<title>UK: BA hints at legal action if no agreement.</title>
<headline>BA hints at legal action if no agreement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways (BA) said on Wednesday that a strike by cabin crew severely disrupting services was unlawful and that it may seek legal redress unless the union involved accepted the deal on offer by 1400 GMT.</p>
<p>BA's director of human resources Mervyn Walker told a news conference that discrepancies in a strike ballot of British Airlines' Stewards and Stewardesses Association (BASSA) members had rendered the strike illegal.</p>
</text>
